# Licensing

This is a multi-licensed repository. There is no single repository-wide
software license. A file's license is determined by the explicit mapping in
[`REUSE.toml`](REUSE.toml), with attribution and provenance recorded in the
owning extension's README and in [`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

- Repository scaffolding, validation tooling, and `apple-wloc` use the MIT
  License. The complete project MIT text is in
  [`LICENSES/MIT.txt`](LICENSES/MIT.txt); retained upstream MIT notices are in
  [`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
- The original `bilibili-cleaner` native work uses `GPL-3.0-only`; its final
  bundle is mapped as `GPL-3.0-only AND BSD-3-Clause` because it retains
  Google's 2008 `goog-varint` code. Distributed corresponding source also
  retains independently licensed MIT `fflate`, Apache-2.0 `protobuf-ts`, and
  the BSD-3-Clause `protobufjs-utf8` component. `REUSE.toml` is authoritative
  for those file-level boundaries. The complete GPL text is in
  [`LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt`](LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt), and BSD texts are in
  [`LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt`](LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt) and the owning
  extension's `source/licenses/` directory.
- `youtube-cleaner` uses `Apache-2.0`. The complete text is in
  [`LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).
- `ad-platform-blocker`, `httpdns-interceptor`, and
  `testflight-region-unlock` are KeleeOne-derived adapted material under
  `CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0`. The complete text is in
  [`LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt).

One extension's license never overrides another extension's license. A
repository-level license found in a mirror also does not override a more
specific license supplied by the original author of a mirrored file. See
[`KELEEONE-LICENSE.md`](KELEEONE-LICENSE.md) for the deliberately narrow scope
of the KeleeOne license boundary.
